    <detaileddescription>
<para>Utility class providing generic functions for UTF conversions.</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Utf" kindref="compound">sf::Utf</ref></computeroutput> is a low-level, generic interface for counting, iterating, encoding and decoding Unicode characters and strings. It is able to handle ANSI, wide, latin-1, UTF-8, UTF-16 and UTF-32 encodings.</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Utf" kindref="compound">sf::Utf</ref>&lt;X&gt;</computeroutput> functions are all static, these classes are not meant to be instantiated. All the functions are template, so that you can use any character / string type for a given encoding.</para>
<para>It has 3 specializations: <itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Utf" kindref="compound">sf::Utf</ref>&lt;8&gt;</computeroutput> (with <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacesf_1af8632a98df098830707aa50ab82029b8" kindref="member">sf::Utf8</ref></computeroutput> type alias) </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Utf" kindref="compound">sf::Utf</ref>&lt;16&gt;</computeroutput> (with <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacesf_1a99b0ac57adecd5594ce6dda56bfe6f70" kindref="member">sf::Utf16</ref></computeroutput> type alias) </para>
</listitem>
<listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="classsf_1_1Utf" kindref="compound">sf::Utf</ref>&lt;32&gt;</computeroutput> (with <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacesf_1a3f2bd4822b2d2563557e3d1d400f6cb8" kindref="member">sf::Utf32</ref></computeroutput> type alias) </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
